# Async conventions

Never block on async work.

**Do not use:**
- `.GetAwaiter().GetResult()`
- `.Result`
- `.Wait()`
- `Task.Run(...)` solely to call async code from sync code

**Prefer:**
- `async`/`await` end-to-end
- `async void` only for UI event handlers (tray menu, buttons) where the signature cannot be `async Task`
- `Dispatcher.InvokeAsync` / `await` when marshaling to the WPF UI thread

When calling async services from a timer or background thread, use `Dispatcher.InvokeAsync(() => coordinator.MethodAsync())` and discard the returned `DispatcherOperation` with `_ =` — do not block waiting for it on the timer thread.
